1. Login

When you log in to AWS, there are mainly two types of users shown:

👑 Root User
The main owner account.
Created when you first register for AWS.
Has full access to AWS services and billing.
Should not be used for daily work.

====

👤 IAM User

IAM = Identity and Access Management

An IAM user is created by the Root User or administrator.
Used for secure access to AWS.
Permissions can be controlled.
Example: one user may get access only to S3, while another gets access to EC2.

===

Simple flow
AWS Account
     │
     ├── Root User 👑
     │      └── Full control
     │
     └── IAM User 👤
            └── Limited permissions based on role

===

